{"step_index":122,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-15T20:24:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-16T01:54:44+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-16T01:54:53+05:30\nThe search for \"\"whiteboard animation\" github cli python OR nodejs \"VideoScribe\" alternative stars\" returned the following summary:\nFor those seeking open-source alternatives to **VideoScribe** or looking to build programmatic whiteboard animations using Python or Node.js, several options exist on GitHub.\n\n### **Notable Open-Source Whiteboard Animation Tools**\n*   **[Inkplainer-OS](https://github.com/NadirWeb-App/Inkplainer-OS)**: A browser-based, open-source tool designed specifically as an alternative to VideoScribe and Doodly. It allows you to convert images and text into whiteboard-style explainer videos with multiple animation styles (e.g., hand-drawn reveal, contour, scanner) and exports to MP4/WebM[1][2].\n*   **[OpenDoodler](https://github.com/Rsverma/OpenDoodler)**: A C#/.NET-based desktop application that allows you to compose SVG and text graphics on a canvas, animate them stroke-by-stroke, and export the result as an MP4 video[3][4].\n\n### **Programmatic & AI-Driven Approaches**\nIf you prefer a CLI-based or programmatic approach, these projects leverage Python and computer vision:\n*   **[handanim](https://github.com/subroy13/handanim)**: A Python library that enables you to programmatically create whiteboard-style animations. It provides an API to animate hand-drawn diagrams, geometric shapes, and text, with exports to MP4 or SVG[5].\n*   **[whiteboard-animation-engine](https://github.com/haseebuchiha/whiteboard-animation-engine-first-video)**: A Python-based engine that automates the generation of explainer videos. It uses computer vision (SAM, GroundingDINO) to process images and create a \"hand-drawn\" animation pipeline[6].\n*   **[ai-img2sketch](https://github.com/daslearning-org/ai-img2sketch)**: A Python-based tool (with a Gradio UI) that converts images into whiteboard sketch animations using NumPy and OpenCV, without requiring heavy pre-trained models[7][8].\n\n### **Collaborative/Interactive Whiteboard Projects**\nIf your g\n<truncated 2104 bytes>\n78mKgYtIsJfQ==)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFmiaohFIa1N6kNnAF4MR2CGjMFkS6AcQxWiEfKD2ctWJw3z5HJugYdFqus6e1q7eUk25gexnKsg4gR0nsq168mL6sOcn984Byd2Cn-SsELSF5iOzPbsOqblI8m3A==)\n[5] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFl5Y6anstO4D42hderWIZI8t3dUKvKQQujwlu16hOxtgBSs6V0YkX4UTfr4bdGZnNBGKj4-8Zyd8jylYamdoZTpSIk2cEX5aiUV5fVD1SJRMylvyZVGAsKRrQ=)\n[6] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFTe330KgmKlPvAjKzrb9g2ogl_q35XTfIKVt4R_jaEY0TXpDDHXEzx_vLd8kLMNVRibSZKs3sMOM2n24bQuuWOxiE-FlnvND4j74TSEkHciXLIHnNFt5hnG5g4RXePgL4Da-CN2JZB1yxeLi7-aCsOIECoAbOayfNmWBbZ6w==)\n[7] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFC2KevofuyuqPKGSu6SIl4kFkgJvgaMehDyJofDAIGGqVrxuvqUVzw8PgoS8Cq0NLWLa_GRJkVbz3wA9JCv5_wFCtqoDlXLMzxJF5EaZDFNCBWoWosfXnGpU0WPCP6-g8eNLiWqjQ=)\n[8] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFC2KevofuyuqPKGSu6SIl4kFkgJvgaMehDyJofDAIGGqVrxuvqUVzw8PgoS8Cq0NLWLa_GRJkVbz3wA9JCv5_wFCtqoDlXLMzxJF5EaZDFNCBWoWosfXnGpU0WPCP6-g8eNLiWqjQ=)\n[9] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG_axhPTww1G7Nm_zMv3WPSxegYHNsH7DicgL7nV_odIRKW5TvDkKxgd-Vvn1Jp1sgBaHkzt9SEpUcuaEim0uQZOP6sRd0eszArngMS6nLm0Q4WVG-Y-T8OTbJx7BRjz44=)\n[10] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHbvgVCrYOsbCsXo-lGtYyZEyuNd3wuritOFPG4BvK7umzS0koi4Cmt3aPRlOMw5z1y7GbLLtsyT90L2Ukr7aR1c5quADNSSXAOarT8I0U-jOWj-GLpCZMZM1CtkefoNQ==)\n[11] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGzcaW-dQwIkcYe-McHQayhgvrASvOFO1vR0benmi4NpUJsw6D0ljNfA-zzoyo6vpyO8CsyLZ0qdyovSdtL8VvlWktzesrEMQKvjm7LujD